# Git workflow (HomeMealCraft)

- Work **only on `main`** unless the user explicitly asks for a branch.
- After finishing a coherent set of changes (feature, fix, docs), **commit and push** to `origin/main` without waiting to be asked.
- Never commit secrets: `.env`, tokens, credentials, local DB files under `data/*.sqlite`.
- Follow the repo commit style: short imperative summary of *why*.
- Do not amend pushed commits; do not force-push to `main`.
- Typical sequence: `git status` → `git diff` → `git add` (relevant files) → `git commit` → `git push origin main` → `git status`.
- Remote: `https://github.com/AlesBan/homemealcraft.git`
